- op: discuss  # cfe5
  at: '2026-09-20T04:22:20Z'  # cfe5
  by: agent  # cfe5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cfe5
  clock: 4  # cfe5
  nonce: cfe5  # cfe5
  message: "SATISFIED. Both readers now delegate to ir.callee_name_of, whose order is meta['callee_name'] -> dst_ref.name -> symbol_name_slot(dst), returning \"\" rather than the raw id when the id yields nothing (symbol_name_slot's own contract: \"\" means no name information, and an unreadable name must not compare equal to a readable one).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE.\n1. The filed repro, re-run on the same artifact with the fix in place: readers disagree on 0 of 74,816 external-dst edges, down from 12. All 12 escaped-name edges now read losslessly (String::from_utf8, not String..from_utf8).\n2. The missed demotion, as a production-path test that fails without the fix: test_finalize_superseded_stubs.py::TestTheCalleeNameIsReadFromItsLosslessHome::test_an_escaped_name_still_reaches_its_demotion. A stub whose id slot escaped '::' to '..', carrying the lossless name in meta and no dst_ref (the WI-huzuv sentinel cell), is now demoted by a resolved edge naming the same method; before the fix last_segment('.') read the stub as 'wrap' and the target as 'Result::wrap' and the comparison failed. Red before, green after.\n3. test_lossless_callee_name.py::TestOneReaderForOneFact pins the agreement itself on the production shape, plus the dst_ref branch and the malformed-id contract.\n\nSCOPE, stated rather than implied. io_boundary._extract_callee_name is NOT folded in: it takes an id STRING, so it can consult neither meta nor dst_ref, and is an id parser rather than an edge reader. The double-span external id shape (rust:external:0-0:Stdio:0-0:null:external_symbol), where symbol_name_slot gives 'Stdio:0-0:null' and a positional read gives 'null', is settled in practice by the chain — a real edge of that shape carries meta['callee_name'] and both readers agree there — but the id shape itself is not addressed here and no claim is made about it.\n\nFull affected slice green: 12 chunks, 21,643 tests, 0 failures; 100% coverage on ir.py, finalize.py and verify_claims.py. Unblocks WI-hupod (ADR-0057 section 15), which needs both the meta and dst_ref branches."  # cfe5
